The program also includes three methods for performing basic arithmetic operations: addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division. These methods use a simple parsing approach to extract the operands from the input string and perform the operation.

Note that this program assumes that the input string will always be well-formed (i.e., each token will either be an operand or an operator). It also includes some error checking to ensure that operations are performed correctly in case of division by zero.
