In the `main` method, the program creates a test board and performs all possible moves for each piece on the board. It then checks if the final state matches the expected output using the `pieceMoveEquals` method.

Note that this program assumes that the input strings will always be well-formed (i.e., each token will either be an operand or an operator). It also includes some error checking to ensure that pieces can only move to valid positions on the board.
